course: dictionary
lesson: 14705
title: Words for chance
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Probability is a word for how likely something is to happen. In maths it is a number from 0 to 1, where 0 means impossible and 1 means certain. A probability can also be written as a fraction or a percentage. «There is a high probability of rain this afternoon.» The words high probability tell you rain is likely.
explain: You can often work out a probability by counting. Probability = the number of ways something can happen ÷ the total number of equally likely outcomes. «The probability of rolling a 3 on a dice is 1/6.» A dice has 6 faces, and only one of them shows a 3.
explain: Probability is also a useful everyday word. «In all probability, the bus will be late» means the bus will very likely be late. In all probability is a formal phrase, so you may meet it in books and on the news. When you see it, swap in very likely and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Probability tells you how likely something is to happen.
fact: On a probability scale, 0 means impossible and 1 means certain.
fact: «Probability» can be written as a fraction, a decimal or a percentage.
fact: A fair coin has a probability of 1/2 of landing heads, which is an even chance.
fact: «In all probability» means very likely.
exercise: «There is a high probability of rain this afternoon.» What does probability mean here? | The number of raindrops in a day | *The chance that something will happen | A kind of umbrella
exercise: A fair coin has a probability of 1/2 of landing heads. What does 1/2 tell us? | It lands heads one time out of ten | It can never land heads | It is certain to land heads | *It is an even chance, like a half
exercise: On a probability scale from 0 to 1, what does 0 mean? | *Impossible | Certain | Very likely | An even chance
test: «In all probability, the bus will be late.» What does in all probability mean? | Not at all likely | *Very likely | Certain to be early | Only just possible
test: What is the probability of rolling a 3 on a fair dice? | 1/3 | 1/12 | 1/2 | *1/6
exam: A dice has 6 equally likely faces. Which sum gives the probability of rolling a 3? | 6 ÷ 1 | *1 ÷ 6 | 3 ÷ 6 | 1 ÷ 3
